---
import '../styles/office.css';

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  current?: 'home' | 'spec' | 'generate' | 'validate';
}
const { title, description, current } = Astro.props;
const nav = [
  { id: 'spec',     href: '/spec/0.1/',  label: 'specification' },
  { id: 'generate', href: '/generate/',  label: 'generate' },
  { id: 'validate', href: '/validate/',  label: 'validate' },
  { id: 'schema',   href: '/schema/vgp-0.1.schema.json', label: 'schema' },
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="giving" type="application/json" href="/.well-known/giving.json" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Spline+Sans+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
  />
</head>
<body>
<!--
  DIRECTION CONTRACT — verifiedgiving.ai

  THESIS: A standards office, not an authority. VGP publishes a grammar that every
  nonprofit applies to its own domain, and this site refuses the dark developer
  landing page with its syntax-highlighted hero and capability cards.

  OWN-WORLD: Socialist kiosk print. Three permitted inks on recycled board —
  #0424AA structural, #00C9FF state, #FFCA0A reserved solely for authorised — with
  an unsigned geometric office mark, hard 2px keylines, no radius, no shadow,
  Archivo locked to a 4px grid, Spline Sans Mono for every path and field name.

  STORY: A developer understands that the nonprofit's own domain is what authorises
  a donation pathway, believes this takes an afternoon rather than a quarter, and
  leaves with a valid giving.json served from their client's site.

  FIRST VIEWPORT: Recycled board, ruled masthead, then the file itself as the
  largest printed cell — giving.json set as printed matter with its authorised
  destination marked in ink 3 — and beside it the kiosk grid where an undeclared
  destination prints as an empty ruled box, never an error. Primary action is a
  printed plate, not a pill.

  SIGNATURE INTERACTION: The register's rows and the file are one object. Focusing
  a destination row shifts its cell one pixel off-register, the way a second press
  pass lands, and marks the corresponding line in the file. Absence is rendered as
  a void in the run, never as a failure state.

  FORM: Socialist kiosk print — dealt as a catalog challenger, taken over the
  assigned direction (index 7 of seven grounded candidates, the transit standards
  manual) on the user's steer. Seed key 8ba41904. Raised four times from the
  declined hand: single-accent totality, structural honesty, density courage,
  numbered units.

  FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster carrying its provenance
-->
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<header class="masthead">
  <div class="plate masthead__inner">
    <a class="masthead__id" href="/">
      <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="1" y="1" width="24" height="24" />
        <path d="M6 13h14 M13 6v14" />
        <circle class="fill" cx="13" cy="13" r="3.2" />
      </svg>
      <span class="masthead__title">Verified Giving Protocol</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary">
      {nav.map((n) => (
        <a href={n.href} aria-current={current === n.id ? 'page' : undefined}>{n.label}</a>
      ))}
      <a href="https://github.com/WholeWhale/verified-giving-protocol">source</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main">
  <slot />
</main>

<footer class="colophon">
  <div class="plate">
    <div class="colophon__row">
      <span>Verified Giving Protocol 0.1 &middot; draft</span>
      <span>Issued by Whole Whale</span>
      <span>MIT licensed</span>
      <span>Last updated 2026-08-27</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/WholeWhale/verified-giving-protocol">Repository</a>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:70ch">
      VGP has no standards-body status and no IANA registration. It is a 0.1 draft.
      It asserts nothing about organisations that have not published a declaration,
      and a destination absent from a declaration is not thereby illegitimate.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
